Fillets: a corner of PerformMoreThreeCorner whose set-back along a sharp
edge passes the edge's other vertex walks over that vertex onto the edge
that goes on along it, where the face on the other side goes on
tangentially across the third edge there (mitcad#2018).

A bent guide (a round tube with a flat top, swept through a quarter turn,
a straight pad at each end) with ribs on the flat, the rib nearest each end
standing 1 degree from the bend's end: the rounding of a rib's sloped edge
ends at the flat's rim, where the rib's sloped side goes on tangentially
into the tube, and PerformMoreThreeCorner fills the corner there with a
plate whose points on the sharp edges are set back by the largest distance
of the stripe's ends from the vertex, 0.508. Along the rim (the edge
between the flat and the tube) that is past the rim's other end where the
pad begins, at a bend radius below about 31 (the rim 1 degree long, 0.49 at
a radius of 30): the plate's point lay off the edge, and the fillet gave an
invalid shape (from 27 to 30.5) or a body left open (26 and less). At that
end vertex the rim goes on tangentially along the pad (the flat is one face
over both), and the tube goes on tangentially across the bend's end edge
into the pad's cylinder.

- WalkOverVertex: whether a sharp edge E between faces Fa and Fb ends at a
  vertex V2 with three edges: E, an edge E2 of Fa that goes on along E (at
  an angle of pi), and an edge Eg between Fb and a face Fc of E2 across
  which Fb goes on tangentially.
- PerformMoreThreeCorner, after its parse, where no two stripes are next
  to each other (the set-back then is the largest distance of the stripes'
  ends from the vertex) and the corner has no free border, seam or two
  tangent stripes: a sharp edge between two sharp edges, shorter than the
  set-back, that WalkOverVertex accepts, with E2 longer than the rest of
  the set-back, is replaced in the corner's edges by Eg and E2 (Eg on the
  side of Fb, Fc between them). Their near vertex is V2: their parameters
  at the vertex, their directions, the orientation of the curves along
  them and the battens' end constraints are taken there instead of at the
  corner's vertex; E2's point is the rest of the set-back along it from V2.
- The plate's border on the side of Fb crosses Eg between the nearest
  points of Eg to the border's two ends (the point of the edge beyond and
  the point on E2), weighted by their distances; where that lies within ten
  times the approximation tolerance (1e-4) of V2, at that tolerance from
  V2: a border through V2 itself runs along E, which the builder then
  keeps in the face beyond as a dangling edge.
- Elsewhere nothing changes. No catch is added.

Test: geometry.fillet_corner_walk_over_vertex
(geometry/tests/test_fillet_corner_walk_over_vertex.cpp) with the case
fillet-corner-walk-over-vertex of MITCAD_GEOMETRY_CASES, and
cli.fcstd_bend_reported (tools/cli/fcstd-bend-reported-test.cmake), the
reported bent guide with its bend radius set to 20, 24, 25, 30 and 32.

